# Context

## Background
Plan 002 (plans/002-decisions-api.md) added the OpenAI Decisions API
as a typed-decision contender against Luna and jev, using the frozen
256-item sample from the September 30 controls run.

## Why This Way
The render helpers were renamed to provider-neutral names instead of
duplicating them, and the output stayed byte-identical. The prompt
fingerprint (4aec9254...) is unchanged, so the Decisions run merges
with the controls in one report without a protocol-mix flag.

## Gotchas
- The endpoint caps `choices` at 255; the 12 items with 256 or more
  options get provider rejections and return no usage, so recorded
  spend ($0.0187722) is an incomplete known subtotal.
- Four S5 no-good items returned refusal answers; these count as
  malformed, not wrong.
- The guide does not document the usage object, so the adapter accepts
  either field naming (input_tokens/output_tokens or
  prompt_tokens/completion_tokens) and the accounting stop blocks
  scored requests when usage stays unknown.
- The contender is gated on OPENAI_API_KEY and never runs by default.

